sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Client / User
    participant Frontend as Next.js App (Client Core)
    participant AuthAPI as Express Auth API (/api/auth)
    participant DB as MongoDB (User, AuthToken)

    %% Login Flow
    Note over User,DB: 1. Login & Token Issuance
    User->>Frontend: Enters Email & Password
    Frontend->>AuthAPI: POST /api/auth/login { email, password }
    AuthAPI->>DB: Query User (select +passwordHash)
    AuthAPI->>AuthAPI: bcrypt.compare(password, passwordHash)
    alt Invalid Credentials
        AuthAPI-->>Frontend: 401 Unauthorized
        Frontend-->>User: Display error message
    else Valid Credentials
        AuthAPI->>AuthAPI: Generate Access Token (15m, typed, sub, role, authVersion)
        AuthAPI->>AuthAPI: Generate Refresh Token (7d, cryptographically random)
        AuthAPI->>DB: Store hashed Refresh Token & update lastLogin
        AuthAPI-->>Frontend: Set-Cookie: token, refreshToken (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite) + Body: { user }
        
        %% Role-based Routing
        Note over Frontend,User: 2. Smart Client-Side Role Redirection
        alt user.role == "system_admin"
            Frontend-->>User: Navigate to /admin (System Admin Dashboard)
        else user.role == "provider_admin"
            Frontend-->>User: Navigate to /provider (Provider Workspace)
        else user.role == "user"
            alt user.region is empty
                Frontend-->>User: Navigate to /profile (Region Onboarding Required)
            else user.region is present
                Frontend-->>User: Navigate to /dashboard (User Dashboard)
            end
        end
    end

    %% Token Refresh Flow
    Note over Frontend,DB: 3. Silent Access Token Refresh
    Frontend->>AuthAPI: POST /api/auth/refresh (Cookie: refreshToken)
    AuthAPI->>DB: Validate stored token hash & check User.authVersion
    alt Token expired or authVersion revoked
        AuthAPI-->>Frontend: 401 Session Revoked
        Frontend-->>User: Redirect to /login
    else Token valid
        AuthAPI->>AuthAPI: Issue new Access Token + Rotate Refresh Token
        AuthAPI-->>Frontend: Return fresh token & updated Cookie
    end
